 "questions": [
  {
   "xml_index": 1,
   "xml_name": "PS3_001_Print Two Lines",
   "display_name": "Print Two Lines",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's start by showing a message on the screen.</p>\n<p><b>Remember:</b> <code>print()</code> shows on the screen whatever you put inside the brackets. Text must be written inside double quotes. Each <code>print()</code> starts a new line. For example:</p>\n<pre>print(&quot;Good Morning&quot;)\nprint(&quot;Have a nice day&quot;)</pre>\n<p>shows this on the screen:</p>\n<pre>Good Morning\nHave a nice day</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a program that prints exactly these two lines:</p>\n<pre>Python is fun\nI can do this</pre>\n<p>(Capital P and capital I, one space between words, and nothing else.)</p>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "Python is fun\nI can do this",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "xml_index": 2,
   "xml_name": "PS3_002_Greet With Full Name",
   "display_name": "Greet With Full Name",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Imagine you are welcoming new students on their first day at Hogwarts, and you greet each one by their full name.</p>\n<p><b>Remember:</b> <code>input()</code> waits for the user to type something, and gives you what they typed. Every <code>input()</code> reads <b>one line</b>. You can keep it in a variable, like this:</p>\n<pre>city = input()</pre>\n<p><code>print()</code> can show several things together if you separate them with commas. It puts one space between them. For example, if <code>city</code> holds <code>Goa</code> and <code>state</code> holds <code>India</code>, then</p>\n<pre>print(&quot;I live in&quot;, city, state)</pre>\n<p>shows <code>I live in Goa India</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a program that reads a first name (on the first line) and a last name (on the second line), and prints <code>Hello</code> followed by the first name and the last name.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> if the user types</p>\n<pre>Harry\nPotter</pre>\n<p>your program should print</p>\n<pre>Hello Harry Potter</pre>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "Harry\nPotter",
     "expected": "Hello Harry Potter",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "Hermione\nGranger",
     "expected": "Hello Hermione Granger",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "Ron\nWeasley",
     "expected": "Hello Ron Weasley",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "Luna\nLovegood",
     "expected": "Hello Luna Lovegood",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "",
