  {
   "xml_index": 3,
   "xml_name": "PS3_003_Cost Of Pens",
   "display_name": "Cost Of Pens",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Imagine one pen costs 12 rupees, and you want to know how much you must pay for some pens.</p>\n<p><b>Remember:</b> <code>input()</code> always gives you text, even when the user types a number. To do maths with it, change it into an integer with <code>int()</code>. For example, this program reads a number and prints double of it:</p>\n<pre>n = int(input())\nprint(n * 2)</pre>\n<p><code>*</code> is used for multiplication.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a program that reads how many pens you buy (a non-negative integer, int &gt;= 0), and prints the total cost in rupees.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> if the user types</p>\n<pre>3</pre>\n<p>your program should print</p>\n<pre>36</pre>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "3",
     "expected": "36",
     "extra": "",
