  {
   "xml_index": 4,
   "xml_name": "PS3_004_Square Garden",
   "display_name": "Square Garden",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Imagine you have a square garden. You want to put a fence around it, and plant grass inside it.</p>\n<ul><li>The length of fence you need is the <b>perimeter</b>: 4 * side</li><li>The amount of grass you need is the <b>area</b>: side * side</li></ul>\n<p><b>Remember:</b> you can do maths on numbers and print the result directly. For example, if <code>n</code> holds <code>5</code>, then <code>print(n + 1)</code> shows <code>6</code>. Two <code>print()</code> lines show two lines of output.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a program that reads the side of the square (a positive integer, int &gt; 0), and prints the perimeter on the first line and the area on the second line.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> if the user types</p>\n<pre>5</pre>\n<p>your program should print</p>\n<pre>20\n25</pre>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
