  {
   "xml_index": 5,
   "xml_name": "PS3_005_Minutes To Hours",
   "display_name": "Minutes To Hours",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A movie runs for some minutes, and you want to say how long it is in hours and minutes. For example, 135 minutes is 2 hours and 15 minutes.</p>\n<p><b>Remember:</b> <code>//</code> divides and keeps only the whole part, and <code>%</code> gives the <b>remainder</b> after dividing. For example, <code>17 // 5</code> is <code>3</code> and <code>17 % 5</code> is <code>2</code> (because 17 = 3 * 5 + 2).</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a program that reads a number of minutes (a non-negative integer, int &gt;= 0), and prints the hours and the leftover minutes on one line, separated by one space.</p>\n<p><b>Example 1:</b> if the user types</p>\n<pre>135</pre>\n<p>your program should print</p>\n<pre>2 15</pre>\n<p><b>Example 2:</b> if the user types</p>\n<pre>45</pre>\n<p>your program should print</p>\n<pre>0 45</pre>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
