  {
   "xml_index": 6,
   "xml_name": "PS3_006_Last Digit",
   "display_name": "Last Digit",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Every positive integer has a last digit: the last digit of <code>1234</code> is <code>4</code>, and the last digit of <code>50</code> is <code>0</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Remember:</b> the <code>%</code> operator gives the <b>remainder</b> after dividing. For example, <code>17 % 5</code> is <code>2</code>. Try a few numbers with <code>% 10</code> and see what you get.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a program that reads a positive integer (int &gt; 0), and prints its last digit.</p>\n<p><b>Example 1:</b> if the user types</p>\n<pre>1234</pre>\n<p>your program should print</p>\n<pre>4</pre>\n<p><b>Example 2:</b> if the user types</p>\n<pre>50</pre>\n<p>your program should print</p>\n<pre>0</pre>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
