  {
   "xml_index": 7,
   "xml_name": "PS3_007_Price After Discount",
   "display_name": "Price After Discount",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A shop gives a <b>15% discount</b> on everything. The price after the discount is:</p>\n<p>price after discount = price - price * 15 / 100</p>\n<p><b>Remember:</b> <code>/</code> gives a decimal number (a float). For example, <code>7 / 2</code> is <code>3.5</code>. Decimal results can have many digits, so round them to 2 digits after the decimal point with <code>round(value, 2)</code>. For example, <code>print(round(3.14159, 2))</code> shows <code>3.14</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a program that reads the price of an item in rupees (a positive integer, int &gt; 0), and prints the price after the discount, rounded with <code>round(..., 2)</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Example 1:</b> if the user types</p>\n<pre>200</pre>\n<p>your program should print</p>\n<pre>170.0</pre>\n<p><b>Example 2:</b> if the user types</p>\n<pre>99</pre>\n<p>your program should print</p>\n<pre>84.15</pre>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
