  {
   "xml_index": 8,
   "xml_name": "PS3_008_Tall Enough To Ride",
   "display_name": "Tall Enough To Ride",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>At an amusement park, you can ride the roller coaster only if your height is <b>at least 120 cm</b> (120 or more).</p>\n<p><b>Remember:</b> to choose between two things to print, use <code>if</code> and <code>else</code>. For example, this program prints <code>Adult</code> if the age is 18 or more, and <code>Child</code> otherwise:</p>\n<pre>age = int(input())\nif age &gt;= 18:\n    print(&quot;Adult&quot;)\nelse:\n    print(&quot;Child&quot;)</pre>\n<p>Notice the <code>:</code> at the end of the <code>if</code> and <code>else</code> lines, and that the lines under them start with some spaces (press the <b>Tab</b> key once). <code>&gt;=</code> means \"greater than or equal to\".</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a program that reads a height in cm (a positive integer, int &gt; 0), and prints <code>Yes</code> if the person can ride, or <code>No</code> if not.</p>\n<p><b>Example 1:</b> if the user types</p>\n<pre>130</pre>\n<p>your program should print</p>\n<pre>Yes</pre>\n<p><b>Example 2:</b> if the user types</p>\n<pre>119</pre>\n<p>your program should print</p>\n<pre>No</pre>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "130",
     "expected": "Yes",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "119",
     "expected": "No",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
