  {
   "xml_index": 9,
   "xml_name": "PS3_009_Positive Negative Or Zero",
   "display_name": "Positive Negative Or Zero",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Every integer is either positive (more than 0), negative (less than 0), or zero.</p>\n<p><b>Remember:</b> to choose between <b>more than two</b> things, use <code>if</code>, then <code>elif</code> (\"else if\"), then <code>else</code>. Python checks them from the top, and runs only the first one that is true. For example:</p>\n<pre>temp = int(input())\nif temp &gt; 30:\n    print(&quot;Hot&quot;)\nelif temp &gt; 20:\n    print(&quot;Warm&quot;)\nelse:\n    print(&quot;Cold&quot;)</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write a program that reads an integer, and prints <code>Positive</code>, <code>Negative</code> or <code>Zero</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Example 1:</b> if the user types</p>\n<pre>15</pre>\n<p>your program should print</p>\n<pre>Positive</pre>\n<p><b>Example 2:</b> if the user types</p>\n<pre>-4</pre>\n<p>your program should print</p>\n<pre>Negative</pre>\n<p><b>Example 3:</b> if the user types</p>\n<pre>0</pre>\n<p>your program should print</p>\n<pre>Zero</pre>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "15",
     "expected": "Positive",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "-4",
     "expected": "Negative",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "0",
     "expected": "Zero",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "1",
     "expected": "Positive",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "-100",
     "expected": "Negative",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
  },
